-- title:
--   Divisorial descent along the resolved Deligne–Rapoport model
-- statement:
--   Let $p\ge 5$ be a prime, let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a `DRModelPackage p` for the two-chart integral model $\mathrm{DRModel}\,p$ of the modular curve over $\mathbb{Z}$, and let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by $p$, with an algebraically closed residue-characteristic-$p$ field $\kappa$ and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa$. Let $\mathfrak{X}_{reg}$ be a `DRResolvedModelPackage` for these data: a scheme $Y$, proper and flat over $\operatorname{Spec} O$, integral and locally Noetherian, with a proper morphism $\mathrm{toDR} : Y \to \mathfrak{X}_O := \mathfrak{X} \times_{\mathbb{Z}} \operatorname{Spec} O$ compatible with the structural maps, regular and of stalk Krull dimension $\le 2$ outside the locus where $p$ is invertible, an isomorphism over $\mathfrak{X}$'s smooth locus and over the generic fibre, together with a finite set of nodes, widths $\ge 1$, a bijection of the nodes with the points of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{compInf}\,\kappa \times \mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{compZero}\,\kappa$, and a family $\mathrm{comp}$ of invertible ideal sheaves indexed by $\mathrm{X0MqComponents}$ of the width function. Assume $\mathfrak{X}_O$ integral; assume (`hrat`) that for every point $x$ of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{compInf}\,\kappa \times \mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{compZero}\,\kappa$ there is a section $s$ of the second projection of $\mathfrak{X}$ base-changed to the residue field of $O$ whose closed point has the same image in $\mathfrak{X}_O$ as $x$. Let $Fc$ assign to each $e$ a family of ideal sheaf data on the standard resolution $\mathrm{Resolution}\,p\,e$ indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}(e+1)$, such that (`hF`) on the $i$-th chart the $k$-th member is cut out by $V$ if $k=i$, by $U$ if $k=i+1$, and is the unit ideal otherwise, transported through the global-sections isomorphism of $\mathrm{CrossingQuotient}\,O\,p$; let $ch$ be a `DRResolvedModelCharts` structure for $p$ and $Fc$, providing étale crossing charts around each node with labels matching $Fc$. Let $\sigma_1,\dots,\sigma_m$ be morphisms $\operatorname{Spec} O \to Y$ sectioning $\mathfrak{X}_{reg}.\mathrm{toBase}$, with exponents $\mathrm{pos}_j,\mathrm{neg}_j \in \mathbb{N}$ and components $v_j$, such that (`hv`) the closed point of each $\sigma_j$ lies in $\mathfrak{X}_{reg}.\mathrm{smoothOffEdges}$, lies in the support of $\mathrm{comp}(v_j)$ and in the support of no other $\mathrm{comp}(w)$. Let $a^{+}, a^{-}$ be natural-number-valued functions on the components, and assume (`hdeg`) that for every node $nd$ and every $i \in \mathrm{Fin}(\mathrm{width}(nd)-1)$ the value at the exceptional component $\mathrm{inr}\langle nd, i\rangle$ of $\sum_j \mathrm{single}\,v_j\,(\mathrm{pos}_j - \mathrm{neg}_j)$ plus the value there of the intersection pairing $\mathrm{intersectionAlpha}$ of the table $\mathrm{x0MqResolvedTable}$ applied to $a^{+} - a^{-}$ vanishes. Then there is a sheaf of modules $M$ on $\mathfrak{X}_O$ that is invertible (each point has an open neighbourhood on which the restriction of $M$ is isomorphic to the unit sheaf) together with an isomorphism between the pullback of $M$ along $\mathrm{toDR}$ and the tensor product, formed by folding over $j = 0,\dots,m-1$, of the dual of the module of $(\ker \sigma_j)^{\mathrm{pos}_j}$ and the module of $(\ker \sigma_j)^{\mathrm{neg}_j}$, tensored with the dual of the module of $\prod_F \mathrm{comp}(F)^{a^{+}_F}$ and the module of $\prod_F \mathrm{comp}(F)^{a^{-}_F}$. Here the module of an ideal sheaf is the kernel of the map from the unit sheaf to the pushforward of the unit sheaf along the closed immersion of the associated subscheme, and its dual is the internal hom into the unit object.
--
--   This is the divisorial case of the descent of line bundles along the resolution of the $A_{e-1}$-singularities of the base-changed Deligne–Rapoport model: a divisorial sheaf built from horizontal sections and vertical components descends as soon as its degree vanishes on every exceptional curve of each resolved crossing chain, the degree being computed by the intersection matrix of the resolved special-fibre table. It is used in the construction of sections of the model with prescribed Abel–Jacobi behaviour, in [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_schemeHomOver_of_comp_eq_zero_of_abelJacobiPin_of_surjective`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_schemeHomOver_of_comp_eq_zero_of_abelJacobiPin_of_surjective).
